# =============================================================================
# DeepSeek-V4-Flash MXFP4 at 262144 -- KV in RAM, experts in VRAM, repacked
# =============================================================================
# The 262144 sibling of `deepseek-v4-flash-128k-kvram`: same three levers
# (-rtr, -nkvo + manual split, big -ub), retuned for the bigger KV.
#
#   MEASURED at 130k depth (RESULTS §12.1), caches on, vs the stock §9.2 config:
#     stock (--fit 8192, caches on)   232.6 pp / 12.36 tg
#     this profile                    402.5 pp / 13.38 tg     +73 % / +8 %
#   The gain is *bigger* than at 128k because --fit is worse here: at margin
#   8192 it leaves only 73.0 GiB of weights on the GPU; the manual split gets
#   89.4 GiB up there, i.e. 16.3 GiB of experts out of DDR5.
#
#   ./serve.sh deepseek-v4-flash-256k-kvram
#   ./serve-deepseek-v4-flash-mxfp4-kvram-256k.sh
#
# Differences from the 128k sibling, all forced by the larger context:
#   * --n-cpu-moe 18, not 17 -- the compute buffer grows with context (2.8 GiB
#     here vs 1.8 at 128k, both ub 2048) and n17 CUDA-OOMs (VERIFIED).
#   * checkpoints cost more here: keeping them costs 24 % generation (17.55 ->
#     13.38), not the ~2 % of 128k -- their overhead scales with the 11 GiB KV.
#     Still ON, because a re-send at 130k depth would otherwise re-prefill for
#     ~5 minutes. For single-shot batch work over huge prompts, override with:
#       IK_EXTRA_ARGS="-mla 3 -fidx --reasoning-format deepseek -nkvo -ctx-ckpt 0 --cache-ram 0"
#
# Same robustness caveats as the 128k sibling: manual placement (~3 GiB VRAM
# free), and -rtr forces --no-mmap so every start re-reads the model.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

: "${IK_MODEL_GLOB:=${IK_MODELS_ROOT}/lmstudio-community/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-MXFP4-00001-of-*.gguf}"

: "${IK_ALIAS:=deepseek-v4-flash-256k-kvram}"
: "${IK_CTX:=262144}"

# Manual split -- --fit would leave 16 GiB of VRAM to rot (see header). Margin
# 4096 does not even load at this context (7.1 GiB compute buffer under --fit).
: "${IK_FIT:=0}"
: "${IK_NCMOE:=18}"

: "${IK_RTR:=1}"
: "${IK_UBATCH:=2048}"
: "${IK_BATCH:=4096}"

# MLA latent cache: f16, never q8_0 (§10.2).
: "${IK_CTK:=f16}"
: "${IK_CTV:=f16}"

: "${IK_EXTRA_ARGS:=-mla 3 -fidx --reasoning-format deepseek -nkvo}"
